{
  "aspect": "9x16",
  "frame": {
    "w": 1080,
    "h": 1920
  },
  "format": "macro",
  "notes": [
    "MACRO, on the v2 plate kit. A print, what it means mechanically, and who",
    "it lands on.",
    "",
    "`who-it-hits` is the one repeat in the vertical formats: four or five",
    "consequences told over TIME rather than as cards in one frame. Three",
    "cards in a 9:16 column measure 33px type, under the readability floor.",
    "",
    "A STATIC PLATE MAY HOLD. The ceiling was written when every plate in the kit boiled; 44 of the 140 are `playback: static` now, because a figure that moves is a figure being re-read. What keeps a data beat short is the ceiling itself, and it is set to what a seventy-second cut of ten beats actually gives each one."
  ],
  "shots": [
    {
      "id": "open",
      "plate": "shorts/hook-card-t3",
      "max_hold_s": 7,
      "anchor": "hook",
      "captions": false,
      "bind": {
        "hook": "script.hook_text",
        "sub": "?script.move_summary",
        "ticker": "script.ticker"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-print",
      "plate": "figures/big-number-l1-9x16",
      "max_hold_s": 7,
      "anchor": "reported",
      "bind": {
        "kicker": "?numbers.headline_kicker",
        "value": "compare.reported",
        "label": "?numbers.headline_label",
        "caption": "?script.move_summary"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "vs-expected",
      "plate": "figures/compare-stacked-9x16",
      "max_hold_s": 7,
      "anchor": "expected",
      "bind": {
        "kicker": "?compare.kicker",
        "label-1": "?numbers.headline_label",
        "value-1": "compare.reported",
        "label-2": "?compare.expected_label",
        "value-2": "?compare.expected"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-statement",
      "plate": "paper/headline-band-t2-9x16",
      "max_hold_s": 7,
      "anchor": "headline",
      "bind": {
        "headline": "script.headlines.0.text",
        "sub": "?script.headlines.0.meaning"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-mechanism",
      "plate": "cards/definition-9x16",
      "max_hold_s": 7,
      "anchor": "turn",
      "bind": {
        "kicker": "?compare.kicker",
        "term": "?numbers.headline_label",
        "body": "script.mechanism.0",
        "example": "?script.mechanism.1"
      },
      "notes": "How it actually works, in the card drawn for a term and its meaning."
    },
    {
      "id": "who-it-hits",
      "plate": "cards/quote-pull-9x16",
      "max_hold_s": 7,
      "anchor": "consequences",
      "bind": {
        "body": "script.consequences.$n-1",
        "attribution": "?script.ticker"
      },
      "repeat": {
        "src": "script.consequences",
        "max": 4,
        "arrange": "sequence"
      },
      "notes": "One consequence per beat, full size. Three in a column measure 33px type, under the readability floor, so a chain at 9:16 has to be told over time."
    },
    {
      "id": "so-what",
      "plate": "structure/both-true-9x16",
      "max_hold_s": 7,
      "anchor": "cheap_or_trap",
      "bind": {
        "kicker": "?compare.kicker",
        "statement-1": "compare.heavy",
        "statement-2": "compare.light",
        "caption": "?script.cheap_or_trap"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "close",
      "plate": "structure/closing-9x16",
      "max_hold_s": 7,
      "bind": {
        "kicker": "?script.ticker",
        "line-1": "script.conclusion",
        "date-label": "?channel.handle"
      }
    }
  ]
}
